{
"from": 169,
"to": 173,
"text": "The block runs, in order: the formatter and the linter; the core crate's and the ledger crate's units; the root binaries' units and the two restore-then-print unit cases (0 selected on the untouched tree); the console binary whole and its two control entries (0 selected on the untouched tree); the help, M3 and M1 counts; the advisory read; the host read; the harness's unit, integration and e2e layers; then the operator pass."
},
{
"from": 175,
"to": 179,
"text": "**What is not run, and why:** no round, no live entry, no live start and no real `claude` (inputs#I1); no mutation run. No new dependency moves (F1), so `cargo deny check` stands as CI's `supply-chain` job, beside the advisory read below that records the chrono re-read. **Boot path:** test-plan declares no boot-path list; by shape `src/main.rs`'s `role_of` and `exit_code` are on every start's path, so the harness smoke trio stands below as operator entries. Every console test starts under a test-owned home and its own PTY."
},
{
"from": 181,
"to": 183,
"text": "**The remove-the-guard controls** are implement's one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries, each on its filtered entry below, `--timeout 900` (a clone build of the root crate and one case). Each case fails on its own bounded wait (12 s `WITHIN`), so a `timeout` reading would NOT read the guard as held."
},
{
"from": 185,
"to": 189,
"text": "| id | File | The edit removes | Case | Entry | |---|---|---|---|---| | `quit-key` | `src/console/` key decoder | the `q` → quit mapping (made unbound) | `console_at_the_floor_logs_a_whole_frame_and_quits_on_q` | `ctl-quit` | | `floor-cmp` | `src/console/` floor rule | `>=` → `>` in the fits comparison against 80×24 | `console_at_the_floor_logs_a_whole_frame_and_quits_on_q` | `ctl-quit` | | `restore` | `src/console/` restore guard | the guard's drop body (made empty) | `console_restores_the_terminal_on_quit` | `ctl-restore` |"
}
],
